1
00:00:56,375 --> 00:00:57,375
Brother.

2
00:00:59,083 --> 00:01:00,083
Sit down, quickly.

3
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:08,040
How do you feel this time?

4
00:01:09,208 --> 00:01:09,750
Good.

5
00:01:10,166 --> 00:01:11,286
A bit better than last time.

6
00:01:24,625 --> 00:01:25,833
Just "a bit"?

7
00:01:27,375 --> 00:01:27,791
What's wrong?

8
00:01:28,375 --> 00:01:29,416
Is there a problem?

9
00:01:31,333 --> 00:01:32,333
With this batch of blood,

10
00:01:32,541 --> 00:01:33,701
I processed and separated it,

11
00:01:34,083 --> 00:01:35,333
and added targeted enhancers.

12
00:01:36,375 --> 00:01:37,625
According to my projections,

13
00:01:38,375 --> 00:01:40,415
you should have stayed
lucid longer than last time,

14
00:01:40,916 --> 00:01:42,836
and the response should
have been much stronger.

15
00:01:46,666 --> 00:01:47,666
Maybe

16
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,125
it just takes time.

17
00:01:52,333 --> 00:01:54,133
Every reaction that
could happen already did.

18
00:01:54,250 --> 00:01:55,833
The data doesn't lie.

19
00:01:57,083 --> 00:01:59,043
You've only maintained
your state from last time.

20
00:02:06,166 --> 00:02:07,246
That's already pretty good.

21
00:02:07,791 --> 00:02:08,333
Brother,

22
00:02:08,625 --> 00:02:09,625
honestly,

23
00:02:10,041 --> 00:02:12,000
it's been a long time
since I felt this clear.

24
00:02:20,458 --> 00:02:22,058
Looks like the dose still wasn't enough.

25
00:02:23,541 --> 00:02:24,541
What?

26
00:02:27,583 --> 00:02:28,583
Nothing.

27
00:04:34,500 --> 00:04:38,500
"The Last Oath"

28
00:04:39,086 --> 00:04:43,586
(Episode 19: Whole Blood Donation Guidelines)

29
00:04:58,666 --> 00:05:00,346
We'll need a much larger volume this time.

30
00:05:00,375 --> 00:05:01,892
There will be loss during
the separation process,

31
00:05:01,916 --> 00:05:03,396
and extraction efficiency is limited.

32
00:05:03,625 --> 00:05:05,040
To maintain the previous results

33
00:05:05,041 --> 00:05:06,161
and keep your brother lucid,

34
00:05:06,583 --> 00:05:07,833
we need even more blood.

35
00:05:09,250 --> 00:05:10,250
I promise you,

36
00:05:10,291 --> 00:05:12,251
not a single drop of your
blood will go to waste.

37
00:05:12,291 --> 00:05:13,691
Every drop will be put to full use,

38
00:05:13,714 --> 00:05:14,714
with maximum efficiency,

39
00:05:14,997 --> 00:05:16,039
to achieve our goal.

40
00:05:20,208 --> 00:05:21,208
Can your body

41
00:05:21,958 --> 00:05:23,083
still handle it?

42
00:05:26,625 --> 00:05:27,625
Do it.

43
00:06:23,793 --> 00:06:25,959
"Lin Zai"

44
00:06:54,833 --> 00:06:55,833
Hang in there.

45
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:23,500
Here.

46
00:07:31,125 --> 00:07:32,125
Take it slow.

47
00:07:32,166 --> 00:07:33,166
No rush.

48
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:44,500
I can take it.

49
00:08:14,625 --> 00:08:15,625
Brother,

50
00:08:17,875 --> 00:08:18,875
I can finally save you.

51
00:08:36,875 --> 00:08:37,875
Give me one too.

52
00:09:03,500 --> 00:09:04,583
Still not used to it.

53
00:09:08,333 --> 00:09:09,333
Some things

54
00:09:10,833 --> 00:09:11,833
you never get used to.

55
00:09:14,041 --> 00:09:15,041
As for this,

56
00:09:16,708 --> 00:09:18,068
I've just gotten accustomed to it.

57
00:10:12,666 --> 00:10:13,166
Lin Zai.

58
00:10:13,541 --> 00:10:15,000
I've made up my mind. Actually, I...

59
00:10:19,416 --> 00:10:20,625
I don't need...

60
00:10:31,583 --> 00:10:32,583
Why do you

61
00:10:34,291 --> 00:10:35,708
smell like He Yao's cigarettes?

62
00:10:36,875 --> 00:10:38,195
Did you pick up smoking from him?

63
00:10:39,666 --> 00:10:40,666
Yeah.

64
00:10:40,750 --> 00:10:42,230
Right now, a cigarette is all I need.

65
00:10:42,458 --> 00:10:43,583
So right now,

66
00:10:43,958 --> 00:10:45,398
the only thing you don't need is me.

67
00:10:48,500 --> 00:10:49,780
Took you long enough to realize.

68
00:12:28,791 --> 00:12:29,791
I don't believe it.

69
00:12:30,458 --> 00:12:31,708
Something must have gone wrong.

70
00:12:35,416 --> 00:12:36,416
It wasn't enough.

71
00:12:36,958 --> 00:12:37,958
Right.

72
00:12:38,291 --> 00:12:39,291
The volume was too low.

73
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:51,208
I want to do it again.

74
00:12:57,333 --> 00:12:58,333
Do it.

75
00:12:59,791 --> 00:13:00,791
Lin Zai.

76
00:13:00,958 --> 00:13:02,958
I need to make the current
situation clear to you.

77
00:13:04,458 --> 00:13:06,458
The antibodies are indeed
becoming more effective,

78
00:13:06,875 --> 00:13:07,875
but inside your brother's body,

79
00:13:07,876 --> 00:13:09,276
a resistance has already developed.

80
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:12,000
It can only temporarily
suppress his frenzy now,

81
00:13:12,333 --> 00:13:14,708
and his lucid intervals
are actually getting shorter.

82
00:13:15,958 --> 00:13:17,198
If we want a real breakthrough,

83
00:13:17,375 --> 00:13:19,775
we have to stimulate his body
to produce its own antibodies.

84
00:13:19,916 --> 00:13:21,436
That requires a massive blood stimulus

85
00:13:21,583 --> 00:13:24,063
to have any chance of breaking
through the resistance barrier.

86
00:13:24,708 --> 00:13:25,708
However,

87
00:13:26,250 --> 00:13:27,892
drawing such large volumes
of blood consecutively

88
00:13:27,916 --> 00:13:29,291
could lead to severe anemia,

89
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:31,000
hypovolemic shock,

90
00:13:31,083 --> 00:13:33,083
or even organ damage.

91
00:13:34,083 --> 00:13:35,083
So I recommend

92
00:13:37,041 --> 00:13:38,041
we halt the experiment.

93
00:13:39,666 --> 00:13:41,583
We can't stop. Absolutely not.

94
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,791
You know my brother is right there.

95
00:13:49,041 --> 00:13:50,249
I can't just stand by when there's hope

96
00:13:50,250 --> 00:13:51,250
and not try to save him.

97
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,000
I can't do that.

98
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:59,000
He Yao,

99
00:13:59,208 --> 00:14:00,208
don't worry.

100
00:14:00,375 --> 00:14:01,375
I can handle it.

101
00:14:07,541 --> 00:14:08,541
All right.

102
00:14:09,125 --> 00:14:10,125
Follow me.

103
00:14:16,583 --> 00:14:17,583
This way.

104
00:14:27,875 --> 00:14:28,875
Lie down.

105
00:14:32,500 --> 00:14:34,140
We're drawing a massive amount this time.

106
00:14:34,458 --> 00:14:35,540
I'll administer IV fluids

107
00:14:35,541 --> 00:14:36,941
to keep your blood pressure stable.

108
00:14:48,375 --> 00:14:49,375
Are you ready?

109
00:14:56,375 --> 00:14:57,375
Let's do it.

110
00:15:07,041 --> 00:15:08,041
Guangqi.

111
00:15:08,166 --> 00:15:09,166
Online.

112
00:15:09,791 --> 00:15:10,791
Scorching Sun reporting.

113
00:15:11,291 --> 00:15:12,666
Immune target lost.

114
00:15:13,666 --> 00:15:14,746
Failed to complete mission.

115
00:15:15,541 --> 00:15:16,833
Synchronizing database.

116
00:15:22,958 --> 00:15:24,083
Mission status updated.

117
00:15:24,375 --> 00:15:25,791
Immune target: Lost.

118
00:15:26,291 --> 00:15:27,291
Please confirm.

119
00:15:28,875 --> 00:15:29,875
Confirmed.

120
00:15:31,041 --> 00:15:32,500
Retrieving relevant protocols.

121
00:15:33,916 --> 00:15:35,375
Sample Escort Protocol notice:

122
00:15:35,708 --> 00:15:37,668
The immune subject is
a critical strategic asset.

123
00:15:37,791 --> 00:15:39,911
Loss will impact subsequent
research and development.

124
00:15:40,375 --> 00:15:42,375
Recommend prioritizing search operations.

125
00:15:42,708 --> 00:15:43,708
I can't find him.

126
00:15:44,291 --> 00:15:45,691
Requesting a new mission directive.

127
00:15:46,458 --> 00:15:47,791
Synchronizing database.

128
00:15:49,916 --> 00:15:51,116
According to mission protocol,

129
00:15:51,166 --> 00:15:52,583
upon loss of the immune subject,

130
00:15:52,833 --> 00:15:55,040
the operative is advised to proceed
to the nearest rendezvous point

131
00:15:55,041 --> 00:15:56,041
to complete handover

132
00:15:56,208 --> 00:15:57,888
and receive directives for the next phase.

133
00:15:58,500 --> 00:15:59,958
Designated rendezvous coordinates:

134
00:16:00,208 --> 00:16:01,625
Latitude 23.1 degrees North,

135
00:16:01,875 --> 00:16:03,625
Longitude 113.2 degrees East,

136
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:06,457
approximately ninety-five
kilometers from your current position.

137
00:16:06,458 --> 00:16:07,833
Recommend proceeding immediately.

138
00:16:16,291 --> 00:16:17,291
Copy that.

139
00:17:41,958 --> 00:17:42,958
Between us,

140
00:17:43,625 --> 00:17:44,625
it's impossible.

141
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:47,833
Everything that happened before,

142
00:17:48,833 --> 00:17:50,166
act like it never happened.

143
00:17:53,875 --> 00:17:55,833
Do you have any idea what I need most?

144
00:17:59,833 --> 00:18:02,458
In such a hurry to leave?
Then go by yourself.

145
00:18:03,750 --> 00:18:04,750
So right now,

146
00:18:05,166 --> 00:18:06,606
the only thing you don't need is me.

147
00:18:08,958 --> 00:18:10,250
Took you long enough to realize.

148
00:18:55,875 --> 00:18:56,875
Lin Zai.

149
00:19:22,100 --> 00:19:24,400
(Antihistamine pills)

150
00:19:39,541 --> 00:19:40,541
Lin Zai.

151
00:19:47,666 --> 00:19:48,666
Have you seen Lin Zai?

152
00:19:48,875 --> 00:19:50,125
Haven't seen him. What's wrong?

153
00:20:06,416 --> 00:20:07,416
Lin Zai!

154
00:20:09,125 --> 00:20:10,125
Lin Zai!

155
00:20:11,666 --> 00:20:12,666
Lin Zai!

156
00:20:15,291 --> 00:20:16,291
Lin Zai!
